WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.400
-So happy you're on the show.
-Me too. Thank you so much.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.534
And what a special night.
My God.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.734
Thank you for
having me here tonight.

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.234
-Yeah, please.
-Thank you all for your service.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.501
Thank you.
-That's pretty cool, right?

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.767
-Yeah, amazing.

00:00:09.767 --> 00:00:11.133
-You know,
we were talking backstage,

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:14.167
and I didn't realize
our paths crossed before,

00:00:14.167 --> 00:00:15.601
as we were struggling.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:18.834
-Yes, before we were, well,
where we are right now, yeah.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:21.334
It was probably
in the late '90s,

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.734
and I saw you at The Improv,

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:25.467
because one of my best friends
was a stand-up --

00:00:25.467 --> 00:00:26.501
Elizabeth Beckwith.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:27.567
-Really?

00:00:27.567 --> 00:00:29.167
-Yeah, we went to
The Improv, and you --

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:31.567
I remember you were playing
guitar to a Troll Doll.

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.634
-Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:33.801
-Everyone starts --

00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:36.133
-And I was like,
"That guy is going somewhere."

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.000
-"He's onto something."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:39.901
-"I hope he gets out of here,
that poor kid."

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:41.300
Yeah, oh, my God.
-No, you were great.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.534
-Oh, please.

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:44.501
You were born and raised
in California.

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.934
-Yeah.
-Do you like coming to New York?

00:00:45.934 --> 00:00:47.567
-I love it. I really do.
I love it.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:49.267
-It's good energy here, right?
-It's so exciting.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:51.367
It really is, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.133
-Do you get to come often?

00:00:53.133 --> 00:00:55.100
-You know,
the last time I was here

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:58.133
was for my birthday in 2019,
and I got to do --

00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:01.133
This may be my
favorite memory of all time.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:03.667
But I got to --
My good friend Regina Spektor

00:01:03.667 --> 00:01:05.634
was doing a residency
on Broadway,

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:06.968
and she invited me to come up

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:08.901
and sing with her
on my birthday.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.133
So I got to be on Broadway,
which was, like,

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:13.334
one of my all-time dreams,
and we got to sing to--

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:15.801
-Did you get nervous?
-Oh, I was terrified. Of course.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:16.901
I mean,
I always get a little nervous.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.067
Like, I'm a little nervous now.

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:20.000
-Yeah, but you had to get
onstage and --

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.400
-Yes. It was amazing, though.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.701
I mean, and everybody sang
"happy birthday" to me.

00:01:22.701 --> 00:01:25.334
The whole audience sang
"happy birthday" to me.

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.167
My parents were in the audience.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.868
You know,
my daughter, her father,

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:30.968
his parents, Regina's parents.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:32.601
-Oh, so it was a family affair.
-Everybody's parents were there.

00:01:32.601 --> 00:01:33.734
You know, it was just, like,

00:01:33.734 --> 00:01:36.300
the most incredible
birthday gift ever.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.467
-I actually got a picture of

00:01:37.467 --> 00:01:38.834
your first visit to
New York City.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:39.934
Is that possible?

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:42.767
-Oh, yes, that is.
That -- Yes, that is it.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:44.567
-This is -- How cool is this
for your first visit

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:45.701
ever going to New York?

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:46.901
-I know exactly where this is.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:49.000
This is the hallway at
"Saturday Night Live,"

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.000
and you're with Molly Shannon
and Will Ferrell.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.868
-Yeah. Yeah.
-There's Will and Molly.

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.901
-The best. Like, how lucky?

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:58.434
-How did you end up here?

00:01:58.434 --> 00:02:00.634
-Okay, so, I had never been
to New York before,

00:02:00.634 --> 00:02:02.434
and I was a theater student,
and I was going, you know,

00:02:02.434 --> 00:02:04.267
in the --
you know, in Los Angeles.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.734
And one of our teachers --
You know,

00:02:05.734 --> 00:02:08.133
I was coming with one of my
friends, Jason, in the picture.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:11.167
And my teacher knew somebody
who worked backstage

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:12.534
in the wardrobe department.

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:14.834
And she was kind enough to say,
"I'll give you a tour,

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.067
and you guys can stay
for rehearsal."

00:02:16.067 --> 00:02:17.467
And we were so excited.

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.200
But when we got there,
we also had tickets

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:22.434
to our first Broadway show,
and we had spent

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:23.634
all of our, you know, like,

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.667
hard-earned
college money on these tickets.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:29.000
So we couldn't stay for
the actual rehearsal,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:31.167
but we got to, you know,
be there and meet everybody.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.801
-You left "Saturday Night Live"
to go see --

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:34.033
-Yeah, I left
"Saturday Night --"

00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:35.200
Okay, wait a second.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.501
I left "Saturday Night Live"
to go see "Cats."

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:40.167
-"Cats."
-Yeah.

00:02:40.167 --> 00:02:42.100
-"Cats." Wow!
-I mean, we had fun.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.267
-No, you've got to go.

00:02:43.267 --> 00:02:44.767
Yeah, everyone's gotta see
"Cats," as well.

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:46.133
-But, yeah, no, probably one of
the dumbest things I've done.

00:02:46.133 --> 00:02:47.701
-And Molly and Will just --

00:02:47.701 --> 00:02:49.167
-They were just crossing.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.334
Like, they were, you know,
going to -- We were all eating.

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.200
I got to eat with everybody,
like, at the --

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.367
I don't know if it was just,
like, tins with spoons and --

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:57.834
-No. That's the Army.

00:02:57.834 --> 00:02:59.901
-Yeah. Well...

00:02:59.901 --> 00:03:03.667
-"Saturday Night Live," we have
catering and I don't know.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.567
-Yeah, so, I got to eat catering
with everybody.

00:03:05.567 --> 00:03:07.200
And it was like --
John Goodman was there.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.901
But the only people
who really stopped

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.567
and took a picture with us
was Will and Molly.

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.534
I mean, they made a point of it.
It was so nice of them.

00:03:13.534 --> 00:03:15.734
And then, who would guess,
years later,

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:19.501
I would play his wife --
twice in, you know, two movies.

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.734
And then he produces our show.
He produces "Dead to Me."

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:25.000
-Oh, no -- And Christina --
-Christina's also his wife.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.901
Yeah, his two wives.
-That's hilarious.

00:03:26.901 --> 00:03:28.367
-Yeah.
-How's Christina?

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.434
How's she doing?
-She's good.

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.667
She says, "Hello."
-Give her my best.

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:32.501
-She said to send her love.
-I love her. Yeah.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.200
"Dead to Me --"
-She's watching.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:36.100
Hi, Christina. We love you.
-Hi, Christina. We do love you.

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:38.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
She is so funny.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.634
-She's the best. She's so good.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:40.734
-Have you worked with
each other before?

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:41.868
-No. We didn't know
each other at all.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:43.067
And, you know,
everyone was like,

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:44.434
"Oh, you guys
are going to love each other."

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:46.200
And, you know, you never know
when you meet somebody.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:47.734
But we just
loved each other instantly

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:49.033
and we were great friends.

00:03:49.033 --> 00:03:52.100
-You can tell you have
great chemistry on the show.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.667
How do we set up the show
without giving away too much?

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.167
-Well, it's nearly impossible.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.901
But, you know, it's the
last season, so Jen and Judy --

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:00.667
If you know the show at all,
we are always kind of

00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.167
in trouble and doing something
we shouldn't be doing.

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:06.167
And the FBI
is following us a bit.

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.367
And so we're on this wild ride
this season,

00:04:09.367 --> 00:04:11.267
sort of finishing up the series.

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.667
-Yeah,
and there's a lot of twists.

00:04:12.667 --> 00:04:14.200
-There's lots of
turns and twists.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:15.968
-Yeah. Get ready for -- Yeah,
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:17.968
Here's Linda Cardellini in
"Dead to Me."

00:04:17.968 --> 00:04:19.334
Take a look at this.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:20.868
-I know.
We have to talk about it.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.000
-Which part?

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.000
-That Steve's been found.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.667
-Oh.

00:04:24.667 --> 00:04:25.968
Yeah, right.

00:04:25.968 --> 00:04:27.234
-I mean, is it terrifying?

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.767
Yeah. Have I been having
low-grade diarrhea about it?

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:29.801
Sure, I have.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.300
-You have?
-Yeah.

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:32.634
It's nervous poops.

00:04:32.634 --> 00:04:35.033
But I have to tell you,
I've been thinking about it,

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.734
and it might not be the
worst thing that could happen.

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.634
-No. That's true.

00:04:38.634 --> 00:04:40.167
-Okay, when we were
at the hospital,

00:04:40.167 --> 00:04:42.667
I kept having this feeling like
another shoe was going to drop.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:43.767
Although, I never understood
why it's a shoe

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:44.868
or why it's dropping.

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:46.667
I mean,
maybe that's a regional thing.

00:04:46.667 --> 00:04:49.834
Anyway, I was afraid
you were the shoe.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:52.367
-Wait. Me?
How -- how am I the shoe?

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.701
-Well, because of
your injuries and stuff,

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.300
and you were the only other shoe
that I had at the time.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.567
-Okay.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.334
-But then, when Ben told me
about Steve, I was like,

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.968
"Oh, there it is."

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:02.400
-So Steve's the shoe.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:03.501
-Right.

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:07.701
-Linda Cardellini, everybody!

00:05:07.701 --> 00:05:09.400
Season 3 of "Dead to Me"

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.801
premieres November 17th
on Netflix.

